---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import stepDialog from "../assets/connect/step2-dialog-prefilled.jpg";
import stepConnected from "../assets/connect/step3-connected.jpg";
import stepChatEn from "../assets/connect/step4-chat-en.jpg";
import stepSlotsEn from "../assets/connect/step5-slots-en.jpg";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const MCP_URL = "https://mcp.yesmcp.com/mcp";
// Documented install link: opens the Add custom connector dialog with both
// fields prefilled (claude.com/docs/connectors/building/directory-vs-custom).
const CLAUDE_ADD_URL = `https://claude.ai/customize/connectors?modal=add-custom-connector&connectorName=yesmcp&connectorUrl=${encodeURIComponent(MCP_URL)}`;
---

<Layout
  title="Try the yesmcp connector in Claude | yesmcp"
  description="Add the yesmcp connector to your Claude in under a minute: paste one URL, no sign-up, no login. Ask what an MCP connector could do for your business and book a consultation without leaving the chat."
  ogTitle="Try the yesmcp connector in your Claude"
  ogDescription="One URL, no login. Our own business, live inside Claude: services, scenarios for your industry, and real consultation booking."
  path="/connect/"
  alternates={{ en: "/connect/", uk: "/ua/connect/" }}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    {/* Warm up the connection before the Add to Claude click — saves DNS+TLS on the jump. */}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://claude.ai" crossorigin />
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://claude.ai" />
  </Fragment>

  <SiteNav switchHref="/ua/connect/" />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-28 pb-24 sm:pt-36">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-ink-faint uppercase">try it live</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-[clamp(1.8rem,5vw,3rem)] leading-tight font-800">
      Try our connector<br />in your Claude
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      We sell MCP connectors, so we run one ourselves. Add it to your Claude in
      under a minute: no sign-up, no login, nothing to install. It works
      on any Claude plan, including the free one. You will see exactly what your
      own customers would see if your business lived inside an AI chat.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-11">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-600">1. Add the connector</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-yes-deep/25 bg-white/40 p-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-ink-faint uppercase">one click · computer or phone</p>
            <a href={CLAUDE_ADD_URL} class="mt-4 inline-block rounded-full bg-yes-deep px-6 py-3 font-medium text-white shadow-[0_8px_24px_-8px_var(--color-yes)] transition-transform hover:-translate-y-0.5">Add to Claude</a>
            <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
              <li>Press the button. Claude opens the add-connector form with the name and URL <strong class="text-ink">already filled in</strong>, like on the screenshot below.</li>
              <li>Check the fields and press <strong class="text-ink">Add</strong>. Done.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">On a phone Claude can take a few seconds to load, so give the form a moment to appear. Not signed in to Claude yet? It asks you to log in first, then shows the same filled form.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/40 p-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-ink-faint uppercase">if the button opened a plain chat instead</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">That happens when the link lands in the Claude app rather than the browser. Two steps by hand:</p>
            <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
              <li>In Claude: your profile → <strong class="text-ink">Settings → Connectors</strong>.</li>
              <li>Press <strong class="text-ink">Add custom connector</strong>, paste the URL below and confirm.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The connector URL for adding it manually (the button above fills it in for you):</p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/40 px-5 py-4" data-copy={MCP_URL}>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-yes-deep select-all break-all">{MCP_URL}</span>
          <button type="button" data-copy-btn data-done="Copied ✓" hidden
            class="shrink-0 cursor-pointer rounded-full border border-yes-deep/40 px-4 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-yes-deep transition-colors hover:bg-yes-deep hover:text-paper">
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 flex items-center gap-5 rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/40 p-5">
          <img src="/assets/qr/connect-en.svg" alt="QR code opening this page" width="104" height="104" loading="lazy" />
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            Reading this on a laptop, but Claude lives on your phone? Scan the
            code: it opens this page there, with the URL ready to copy.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
          Works on claude.ai, in the mobile apps and in Claude Desktop, on the
          free plan too. ChatGPT users: our app-directory submission is in
          preparation; for now the connector runs in Claude.
        </p>
        <Picture src={stepDialog} formats={["avif", "webp"]} alt="The Add custom connector dialog opened by the button: name and URL already filled in"
          widths={[536, 1072]} sizes="(min-width: 640px) 28rem, 100vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
          class="mt-5 w-full max-w-md rounded-2xl border border-ink/10" />
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-600">2. Allow the tools</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          After adding, press <strong class="text-ink">Connect</strong> on the connector card.
          The permissions screen opens: set <strong class="text-ink">Read-only tools</strong> to <strong class="text-ink">Always allow</strong> so Claude stops asking before every read.
          Leave booking on confirmation: Claude will check with you before it books, which is
          exactly right.
        </p>
        <Picture src={stepConnected} formats={["avif", "webp"]} alt="The yesmcp connector card with tool permissions"
          widths={[640, 960, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 44rem, 100vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
          class="mt-5 w-full rounded-2xl border border-ink/10" />
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-600">3. Ask it something</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Start a new chat and try any of these:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <li class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/40 px-5 py-3 text-ink-soft">“What could an MCP connector do for a <strong class="text-ink">dental clinic</strong>?”</li>
          <li class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/40 px-5 py-3 text-ink-soft">“What does <strong class="text-ink">yesmcp</strong> actually build, and how does an engagement run?”</li>
          <li class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/40 px-5 py-3 text-ink-soft">“Show me yesmcp's free consultation slots and <strong class="text-ink">book one</strong> for me.”</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Here is what it looks like in the chat: Claude calls the connector's
          tools itself and answers from live data.
        </p>
        <Picture src={stepChatEn} formats={["avif", "webp"]} alt="Claude chat: the connector answering about yesmcp services"
          widths={[640, 960, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 44rem, 100vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
          class="mt-4 w-full rounded-2xl border border-ink/10" />
        <Picture src={stepSlotsEn} formats={["avif", "webp"]} alt="Claude chat: live consultation slots with timezones"
          widths={[640, 960, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 44rem, 100vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
          class="mt-4 w-full rounded-2xl border border-ink/10" />
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The booking is real: you pick a live slot, get a confirmation email
          immediately, and we meet you there. Every answer comes from our own
          published content, so the assistant cannot invent prices or promises.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-600">What it knows about you</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Nothing, until you book. A booking stores exactly three things: your
          name, your email address, and the topic you want to discuss. Details in
          our <a href="/privacy/" class="link-und text-ink">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-600">Want one of these for your business?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          This page is the product demo: what you just tried is what we build
          for clients, wired to their real schedule, catalog and orders. Book a
          call right in the chat above, or write to us: <a href="https://t.me/yesmcp_bot?start=connect" class="link-und text-ink">@yesmcp_bot</a>{" · "}<a href="mailto:yes@yesmcp.com" class="link-und text-ink">yes@yesmcp.com</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter switchHref="/ua/connect/" />
  <script is:inline type="module" src="/js/copy-url.js"></script>
</Layout>
